---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CLARITY_ID, CONTACT_EMAIL, GA4_ID, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Legal notice of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: publisher, host, liability`} description="Legal notice of Benefits Calc: publisher Radif Partners, publication director, host, what the benefit calculators are for, limits of liability, reuse of Crown copyright material, law." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Legal notice' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Legal notice</h1>
    <p>Information given under Article 6 III-1 of French law no. 2004-575 of 21 June 2004 on confidence in the digital economy, the publisher being established in France.</p>
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>Publication director: {AUTHOR_NAME}, responsible for the content of {SITE_URL}.</p>
    <h2>Hosting provider</h2>
    <LegalIdentity mode="hosting" lang={lang} />
    <h2>Purpose of the site</h2>
    <p>The site offers free calculators and guides on social security benefits in the United Kingdom. Results are <strong>estimates</strong> made from the answers you give and the 2026/27 rates. They are not advice and do not bind the DWP, HMRC, Social Security Scotland, the Department for Communities or a tribunal. The site is independent and has no link with any of them. Method and limits: <a href={route('method', lang)}>method</a>.</p>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>Figures are re-read at their sources at each change in the law and the calculations are covered by automated tests, without any guarantee that no error remains. The publisher cannot be held liable for a decision taken on the sole basis of a result. Errors can be reported through the <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact</a> page.</p>
    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>Texts, graphics and code belong to the publisher; short quotations with a link to the page are welcome. Crown copyright material and legislation quoted from legislation.gov.uk and GOV.UK are reused under the <a href="https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Open Government Licence v3.0</a>.</p>
    <h2>Embedding</h2><p>The Universal Credit calculator can be embedded free of charge with the credit link kept visible: <a href={route('widget', lang)}>embed page</a>.</p>
    {/* gen-legal-pages:terms */}
    <h2>Personal data and cookies</h2>
    {GA4_ID ? (<p>What you type in the calculators stays in your browser. The site sets Google Analytics audience measurement cookies (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_{GA4_ID.replace('G-', '')}</code>, 13 months at most), with no advertising{CLARITY_ID && '; page stability is monitored with Microsoft Clarity, cookie-free'}. Details, legal basis and how to object: <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> and <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page.</p>) : (<p>What you type in the calculators stays in your browser and the site sets no cookies{CLARITY_ID && '; page stability is monitored anonymously with Microsoft Clarity, cookie-free'}. See the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> and the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page.</p>)}
    {/* /gen-legal-pages:terms */}
    <h2>Reporting unlawful content</h2><p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, with the page address and the reason.</p>
    <h2>Governing law</h2><p>French law. Failing an amicable solution, the courts of {LEGAL.jurisdiction} have jurisdiction, without prejudice to the mandatory rules protecting consumers in their country of residence. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
